{
  "id": "Compound::DB00615 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Rifabutin is known to bind to Cyp1a2, a cytochrome P450 enzyme involved in the metabolism of various substrates, including caffeine and lidocaine. This binding leads to Cyp1a2 participating in metabolic pathways such as caffeine oxidase activity and lidocaine metabolism, both of which are associated with Cyp3a4. The evidence suggests that Rifabutin may indirectly influence Cyp3a4 through the activation of Cyp1a2, which in turn participates in metabolic processes that are linked to Cyp3a4. The shared involvement of Cyp1a2 and Cyp3a4 in these metabolic activities implies a potential mechanistic link between Rifabutin and Cyp3a4, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Rifabutin to Cyp3a4 through Cyp1a2 supports the hypothesis that Rifabutin may modulate Cyp3a4 activity via a metabolic intermediate.",
